<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John of Capistrano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1386–1456</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Saint John of Capistrano, Giovanni da Capestrano</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John of Capistrano was an Italian Franciscan friar and preacher who campaigned across central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussites">Hussites</a> and for a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. In 1456 he raised a crusading army of peasants and townsmen that, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-hunyadi">John Hunyadi</a>'s forces, broke the Ottoman siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a>. He died of plague soon afterwards and was canonised in 1690.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-of-capistrano.jpg" alt="John of Capistrano" width="320" height="705" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:82Johannes_von_Capestrano.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
